Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Caitlin-Clark.md` and appended the `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom. No body edits.

**The two biggest flags:**

1. **The draft skips the two most famous unclosed items on her ledger** — she lost the national championship game twice and never won one, and she was left off the 2024 Olympic team. For a piece whose whole thesis is "the audit never closes," those are the audit. Her own quotes on both are gifts for the Type 1 read (on the Olympic snub she basically conceded the case against herself), and neither appears anywhere.

2. **Angel Reese and the race discourse are entirely absent.** Any reader who knows Clark notices this immediately, and it's the hardest available test of the typing: she's at the center of a racialized fight she didn't start, and her moral account of herself is exactly what's at stake. The draft already has the raw material — "Black women that grew up making this league what it is deserve all the credit" — but files it in the Rabbit Hole as a wing-2 footnote. Swoopes is the safe critic; this is the real one.

Also worth knowing before the next pass: "That is the empathy turn" is house vocabulary sitting on the page, the Bluder-throws-her-out-of-practice fact is referenced three times and never rendered as a scene, and the fingerprint ledger's "0 contrast pairs" undercounts — the same "not X, but Y" move fires four times in four consecutive sections.

Sources for the reality check: [Yahoo Sports on the title losses](https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/caitlin-clark-answers-not-winning-143000121.html), [SI on the Olympic snub reaction](https://www.si.com/onsi/womens-fastbreak/news/caitlin-clark-reveals-raw-reaction-to-team-usa-olympics-snub-01jerjzdgfcg), [Salon on the Clark–Reese discourse](https://www.salon.com/2025/05/28/caitlin-clark-and-angel-reeses-rivalry-reveals-the-ugly-side-of-the-wnbas-rise/), [Hawk Central on the Fever's August 2026 record](https://www.hawkcentral.com/story/sports/college/iowa/basketball-women/2026/08/02/caitlin-clark-stats-points-indiana-fever-minnesota-today/91139388007/).
